A developer is preparing a plain-text subtitle wrapper for an offline editing tool. The input is a list of paragraphs; each paragraph is a string whose words are separated by one or more ASCII spaces. Width is a positive integer. Words are indivisible, an over-width word occupies a line alone, paragraph boundaries must remain visible as blank lines in the output, and the input list must not be mutated. The contract makes no claims about graphemes, font metrics, or non-ASCII whitespace. The developer can supply this flawed implementation:

